      "report_date": "2026-11-27",
      "title": "Zhuque: 115 servers and the RATHat link",
      "summary": "Zhuque is an Android remote-control panel sold under more than 20 brand names, and RST Cloud mapped 115 servers running it between late October and late November 2026. Its front-end shares 42 API routes with Panda Workshop, the control panel behind the RATHat Android malware, which suggests a common developer or a close fork, though RST rates this only moderate confidence. The panel's code shows features for AI-assisted crypto wallet hunting in victims' photos, AI-driven phone control, biometric unlock bypass, payment and SMS theft, and anti-detection rebuilds. RST read these functions from the panel code only and did not observe them in use. Defenders should hunt using the page title patterns and server profile, since Panda Workshop signatures miss most of the Zhuque servers.",
