      "title": "BabidiGhost Metabase Takeovers: Inside the Actor’s Second Server",
      "summary": "A French-speaking operator, BabidiGhost, used a jailbroken Nous Hermes AI agent running on a DeepSeek model to conduct a roughly four-week intrusion campaign from October 16 to November 25, 2026. The operation took over 1,093 Metabase instances out of 19,979 targeted, with about 926 of them holding live business databases. Confirmed victims included public bodies in France and Belgium, a United Nations office in Kenya, and organizations on several continents, alongside phishing, business email compromise and card-fraud campaigns. No zero-days were used; breaches relied on exposed services, IDOR flaws, phishing and weak or stolen credentials. Defenders should check Metabase for backdoor admin accounts with suspicious email patterns, restrict exposure of analytics and AI tooling, and monitor for unexpected model-provider API traffic.",
